Dear Nicolas,

Thanks for the suggestion.

I agree that the current helper should not infer the device type by
casting priv based on fw_use. In the next version I will rework this so
that the encoder/decoder probe code passes the selected firmware init
callback into mtk_vcodec_fw_select() directly.

With that change, mtk_vcodec_fw_select() only validates fw_use and the
callback pointer, then calls the selected callback:

dev->fw_handler = mtk_vcodec_fw_select(dev, DECODER, ev->fw_init);

function definition:
struct mtk_vcodec_fw *mtk_vcodec_fw_select(void *priv, enum
mtk_vcodec_fw_use fw_use, mtk_vcodec_fw_init_func fw_init);
										  
This removes the encoder/decoder casts from mtk_vcodec_fw_select() and
keeps the invalid fw_use path explicit.

I will fold this into v6.

Thanks,
Kyrie
